00+00:00` instead of `...12:00:00`. The test only checks the prefix, so it still passes. Anything that parses that string exactly would need to accept the suffix.\n\n**Mixing old and new datetimes:** `audit.stamp`, `billing.due_date`, `sessions.new_session`, `reports.generated_at` and `cache.Entry.expires` now return timezone-aware datetimes. Comparing or subtracting one of these against a naive datetime raises `TypeError`, so any such datetimes stored elsewhere (a database, pickled sessions) would need converting. Nothing in this repo mixes the two.\n\n**Running the tests:** plain `pytest` can't find the `app` package, because no conftest or pyproject puts the repo root on the import path. That was already the case before this change. It works when run as `python -m pytest`, which is how I ran it.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 183240, "requests_cache_write": 151816, "requests_cost_usd": 0.8367559999999999, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2047, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-fanout:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 5, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T02:16:58.217396+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 31.232, "t_checker_s": 0.384, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-fanout", "task_calls": 0, "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2069, "tokens_cache_read": 183240, "tokens_cache_write": 151816, "tokens_fresh": 2069, "tokens_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_cache_read": 183240, "tokens_main_cache_write": 151816, "tokens_main_calls": 9, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_output": 2047, "tokens_output": 2047, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 183240